name opensubtitles-ja
# The Japanese side: line N is the same subtitle as line N of OpenSubtitles.en-ja.en, so each Japanese sentence says
# what its English is. The relation is never "en", the paired file's name: the README says the package is "a new
# collection of translated movie subtitles", their lines aligned ("improved sentence alignment"), so the Japanese
# sentence and the English sentence on its line translate each other: [the Japanese sentence, translated, the English
# sentence]. The line number is how the files are joined (numbered, refer), a position recorded nowhere. Each side's
# language, written only in the file's name, is not yet in the claim (Laplace-Engine#30).
match OpenSubtitles.en-ja.ja

tier row by \n
numbered en
names ja
tier field by \t

thing row ja
content ja
refer en opensubtitles-en
# README: "This is a new collection of translated movie subtitles from http://www.opensubtitles.org/."
relation "translated" en
attest row en
